        "question_text": "Two resistors of $r$ ohms and $s$ ohms are connected in parallel. Their combined resistance is $\\frac{1}{\\frac{1}{r}+\\frac{1}{s}}$ ohms. Write this as a single fraction.",
        "structure": "fraction-in-denominator",
        "solution_text": "$\\frac{1}{\\frac{1}{r}+\\frac{1}{s}}$\n$=\\frac{rs\\times 1}{rs\\left(\\frac{1}{r}+\\frac{1}{s}\\right)}$\n$=\\frac{rs}{s+r}$ ohms"
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Show that the average of $\\frac{1}{n}$ and $\\frac{1}{n+2}$ can be written as $\\frac{n+1}{n(n+2)}$.",
        "structure": "fraction-in-numerator",
        "solution_text": "$\\frac{\\frac{1}{n}+\\frac{1}{n+2}}{2}$\n$=\\frac{n(n+2)\\left(\\frac{1}{n}+\\frac{1}{n+2}\\right)}{n(n+2)\\times 2}$\n$=\\frac{(n+2)+n}{2n(n+2)}$\n$=\\frac{2n+2}{2n(n+2)}$\n$=\\frac{n+1}{n(n+2)}$"
      }
